From: nancc@netcom.com (Nancie Clark)
Date: Thu, 8 Dec 1994 08:11:02 -0800 (PST)
Subject: [#94-12-329] Media

Interfacing with the media is not new to Extropians.  We have been doing 
it for some time.  I have been interviewed on transhumanism starting five 
years ago.  I have promoted and encouraged the media exposure of 
Extropians belief systems for several years.  Both Max and I have been on 
local and global television, and Max on the radio more times than I can 
think of.  I have been asked to be a guest speaker at at least one 
education foundation, and on the chart to do several others (UC - 
Colorado Art Department - regarding "Live As Art" pertaining to extropian 
transformations, living indefinitely, creating "ourselves" as art.

And, I intend to create more exposure.  Why not?  

Perhaps the question is, "What is the purpose?"  Certainly it is for 
individual recognition as well as recognition of the Extropian movement. 
I have been in the media (television, newspapers, magazine) because of my 
work and career as a performer/artist.  It just happens that today, I 
take more with me -- I take the hope of introducing innovative ideas to 
others about issues which have made my own life more fluid, more rich, 
more adverturesome.

Because we persistently claim to that the "We are all individuals!" (Monty 
Python quote expressed by many), we need to take a look at how our 
individuality affects coverage and how we give our personal "look" to 
Extropian philosophy.  We may not appreciate or even like the approach of 
one another -- the stylistically approach.  Perhaps we may need to pull back 
a bit on some heavily personal stuff to be more empathic to the whole.  

I would like to see numerous hubs of Extropians approaching possible 
media coverage.  Certainly there are many who are photogenic, bright, 
and good at handling the "press".  What's happening on the east coast?  
The south?  I hear through Alcor and Steve Bridge that those in Arizona are 
becoming ole' hands at the media.

Nancie Clark
    

